Z||000000||Fierochic88||07-21-2001||10:45 PM||||Well the day started off long and slow with the installation of a factory sub into my 88GT.  This included rearranging the previously installed alarm system and CD unit that works through the radio.  After taking the sub out 5-6 times when the door lock relays weren't working (only to discover that the battery was low) Dad and I finally got everything put together.  The car looked and sounded great!<P>Of course things can never be easy.  We decided to take my Fiero & Dad's Vette to the local cruise night.  My friend Jason was working on his car and decided he wanted to go so I let him drive Dad's car, the more Fiero's the better!  On the way there this horrible knocking noise started and progressively got worse as we pulled into Pennside Drive In.  Sure enough, it was the rods, and a very dismayed father quickly diagnosed the problem.<P>So now, less than 2 weeks till Williamsburg and Dad's beautiful car needs an engine drop.  So tomorrow at 7 we're going to hopefully pull it before heading down to SkiTime's.  Dad wasn't going to go tomorrow but I convinced him he would be missed and promised to get up early and help him.  So everybody keep your fingers crossed!<P><BR>Jennifer<P>------------------<BR>IM Username:  FieroChic88<BR>Silver 1988 GT<BR>Silver 1986 2m4<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/jenscar-sig1.jpg"> ||||reg||11
